→ warning\n- [x] 1.3 Wire into tier-0 (`just tier0` / main.rs subcommand) and add\n  `ERR_ROUTING_PARITY` reporting; GHA workflows check out the ddl sibling so\n  the gate enforces in CI (warning-only in local standalone clones)\n- [x] 1.4 Expand routing.toml: testaruda, turu(whisper), ah(espectacular\n  exists), pretender, vampiro, incitaciones, openspec (`upstream = true`),\n  specodelic, funkalization, wild, dulce-de-leche, bd (`upstream = true`);\n  verify parity check green\n\n## 2. Tier-0 doc-coverage audit\n\n- [x] 2.1 Failing test: surface extraction — fixture binary `--help` with\n  subcommands/flags → token set (kebab/snake/spacing normalization)\n- [x] 2.2 Implement surface extractor (`src/doc_audit.rs`: Purpose header per\n  e10 Must gate); `surface: none` fixtures skip cleanly\n- [x] 2.3 Failing test: inventory extraction — fixture repo with README +\n  docs/ + llms.txt + AGENTS.md managed block → feature-token set per surface\n- [x] 2.4 Implement inventory scanner; breadcrumb-reachability check\n  (llms.txt / managed blocks) distinguishing ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED vs\n  ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE\n- [x] 2.5 Wire audit rows into report as new check-codes (report_version\n  stays 1, additive); `just tier0` green\n\n## 3. Routing integration for audit faults\n\n- [ ] 3.1 Failing test: audit row with ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED crosses\n  threshold → dry-run proposal with token `evallerina:<scenario>:<fault-class>`\n- [ ] 3.2 Dry-run smoke against latest tier-2 rows; review proposals before\n  any filing (mirrors 4.3 of add-fault-ticket-routing)\n\n## 4. Doc-findability scenarios (first tools)\n\n- [ ] 4.1 Fixture: turu (whisper) repo slice with llms.txt breadcrumb to a\n  seeded feature doc\n- [ ] 4.2 Record live tier-2 transcript; land scenario JSON + tier-1 replay in\n  same commit (design D5)\n- [ ] 4.3 Repeat for testaruda and ah; step budget + discovery-channel row\n  provenance asserted in replay tests\n\n## 5. Edge-exploration scenarios (first tools)\n\n- [ ] 5.1 Failing test: classifier — non-zero exit without hints on\n  undocumented input → ERR_EDGE_UNHANDLED; hint ignored →\n  ERR_ENVELOPE_HINT_BLINDNESS (existing class)\n- [ ] 5.2 Fixtures + recordings for wai and dont edge inputs (existing battery\n  tools first — cheapest provenance)\n- [ ] 5.3 Extend to turu/testaruda/ah recordings as they land\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n- [ ] 6.1 `just tier0` green; routing-parity + doc-coverage gates pass on this\n  repo itself\n- [ ] 6.2 Dogfood first: run the doc-coverage audit against evallerina's own\n  surfaces (README, docs/, AGENTS.md) before any tool-fixture rollout —\n  fastest way to shake out the extractor\n- [ ] 6.3 `just tier1` replay unchanged for existing scenarios\n- [ ] 6.4 One full nightly rotation green with new families; dry-run\n  proposals reviewed; `--file` remains opt-in\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792527941277},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"PWO7Qwd92","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/.wai/projects/evallerina/research/2026-10-20-evallerina-fok-real-ecosystem-audit-breadth.md","offset":1,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":30180,"output":78,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":30258,"cost":{"input":0.0022635,"output":0.0000156,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0022791}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792527941278,"responseId":"gen-1792527941-pcL4GtWl0k5kUKJDQUnr","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"PWO7Qwd92","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research: evallerina-fok — real-ecosystem doc-audit rows exceed follow-up threshold\n\nDate: 2026-10-20 · Ticket: evallerina-fok · Trigger: brief follow-up threshold\n(\"real-ecosystem audit rows exceed ~40 → STOP, record findings, ship mechanism\nagainst fixtures, leave onboarding notes for 73q\").\n\n## Finding\n\n`cargo run -- doc-audit` against the checked-in `doc_audit.toml` yields **91\naudit rows** across 9 tools (threshold ~40). Breakdown:\n\n- `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`: 77 rows — token documented on some surface but not\n  reachable from llms.txt / AGENTS.md managed-block breadcrumbs. Dominant\n  pattern: most repos document commands/flags in README/docs but have no\n  breadcrumb channel (no llms.txt, or llms.txt that doesn't enumerate the\n  feature). This is the *intended* signal of the gate, not extractor noise.\n- `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`: 14 rows — e.g. `dont color/forget/nopersist/quiet/\n  stats`, `turu quiet/verbose/help`, `specodelic verbose/exit1`, `ah help`,\n  `vampiro completions`, `incitaciones dir`, `pretender help`.\n\nProvenance (16/16 tools accounted, **zero silent skips**): 10 `extracted`,\n4 `binary_absent` (genesis, espectacular, funkalization, dulce-de-leche —\nbinaries not on PATH in this checkout), 2 `skip` (bd, openspec —\n`surface = none` by config).\n\nNo tool's `--help` resisted parsing — the general extractor rules (long flags,\nCommands: sections, exit-code sections) harvested all 10 present binaries\nwithout tool-specific cases. The threshold tripped on breadth (row count), not\nparse resistance.\n\n## Decision (per brief)\n\n- Do NOT tune normalization to make real rows vanish (anti-goal).\n- The mechanism ships against fixtures; all contract tests are hermetic\n  (throwaway shell scripts + temp repos). `cargo test` green.\n- Real-tool onboarding for 73q (validation phase): see notes below.\n- The CLI exits 0 on findings — rows are the record (mirrors `report`\n  precedent: findings do not affect the exit code; loud errors exit nonzero).\n  Rows print on every `just tier0` run, so drift is surfaced immediately.\n\n## Onboarding notes for 73q\n\n1. **binary_absent tools**: build/install `genesis`, `espectacular`,\n   `funkalization`, `dulce-de-leche` binaries on PATH (or\n   extend `doc_audit.toml` with explicit `binary` paths into their\n   `target/`) so their surfaces join the audit.\n2. **NOT_FINDABLE triage**: 77 rows mostly mean \"add an llms.txt breadcrumb or\n   managed-block mention per feature\". Recommend each repo owner add an\n   llms.txt enumerating commands/flags; then rows collapse to genuinely\n   undocumented tokens.\n3. **Noise class**: clap auto-generates a `help` subcommand/flag; it shows up\n   as UNDOCUMENTED when docs don't mention \"help\". If 73q wants to suppress\n   it, that should be a *general* normalization decision recorded here — not\n   per-tool tuning.\n4. **Gate posture**: doc-audit rows do not fail `just tier0` (measurement,\n   not gate). If the epic wants a gate later, add a threshold/scoped-gate\n   decision to a follow-up ticket — do not silently tune the extractor.\n\n## Artifacts read/produced\n\n- Produced: `src/doc_audit.rs`, `doc_audit.toml`, `tests/doc_audit.rs`,\n  report wiring in `src/report.rs`, CLI in `src/main.rs`, justfile tier-0 line.\n- Fresh evidence: `cargo test doc_audit` (8 passed) and `just tier0` tails in\n  the evallerina-fok ship record.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792527946482},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"jfa1EOHam","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/src/doc_audit.rs","offset":201,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":31199,"output":47,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":31246,"cost":{"input":0.002339925,"output":0.000009400000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.002349325}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792527946484,"responseId":"gen-1792527946-4VFO2QBl3fiY8cMpsC7F","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"jfa1EOHam","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// Extract the concatenated text of every `<!-- X:START --> ... <!--\n/// X:END -->` managed block in a markdown file — the only part of\n/// AGENTS.md that serves as a breadcrumb channel.\nfn managed_block_text(text: &str) -> String {\n    let mut out = String::new();\n    let mut in_block = false;\n    for line in text.lines() {\n        let lower = line.to_lowercase();\n        if !in_block {\n            if lower.contains(\":start -->\") {\n                in_block = true;\n            }\n            continue;\n        }\n        if lower.contains(\":end -->\") {\n            in_block = false;\n            continue;\n        }\n        out.push_str(line);\n        out.push('\\n');\n    }\n    out\n}\n\n/// Harvest candidate feature tokens from documentation text: long\n/// flags, backtick code spans, hyphenated identifiers, and plain\n/// words, all canonicalized. Deliberately generous (a superset):\n/// extra doc-side tokens never hide a real drift, while a missing\n/// token is what produces an audit row.\nfn harvest_doc_tokens(text: &str) -> BTreeSet<String> {\n    let mut tokens = BTreeSet::new();\n    for line in text.lines() {\n        let line = line.trim();\n        for word in line.split_whitespace() {\n            // Long flags in prose or backticks: `--flag-name`.\n            if let Some(flag) = word.strip_prefix(\"--\") {\n                let flag = flag.trim_matches(|c: char| !c.is_ascii_alphanumeric());\n                if !flag.is_empty() {\n                    tokens.insert(canonical_raw(flag));\n                }\n            }\n            // Strip surrounding code-span backticks and punctuation so\n            // `deploy`, and `tear-down`,` both yield their token.\n            let bare = word.trim_matches(|c: char| !c.is_ascii_alphanumeric());\n            let mut pieces = bare.split(|c: char| !c.is_ascii_alphanumeric());\n            // Hyphenated identifiers (tear-down) are one token; plain\n            // words are harvested per piece.\n            if bare.contains('-') || bare.contains('_') {\n                tokens.insert(canonical_raw(bare));\n            } else if let Some(piece) = pieces.next() {\n                tokens.insert(canonical_raw(piece));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    tokens\n}\n\n/// The two doc-coverage check-codes. `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`: a\n/// surface token absent from every scanned surface. `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`:\n/// a token documented on some surface but not reachable from the\n/// breadcrumb channels (llms.txt / managed blocks).\npub const ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED: &str = \"ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\";\npub const ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE: &str = \"ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE\";\n\n/// One doc-coverage audit row: a surface feature token that is either\n/// undocumented or unfindable. Deliberately per-token — no aggregate\n/// doc-quality score exists (anti-goal, pinned by test).\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]\npub struct AuditRow {\n    pub token: String,\n    pub code: String,\n}\n\n/// Diff a tool's surface tokens against a doc inventory: absent from\n/// all surfaces → `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`; present on some surface\n/// but unreachable from breadcrumbs → `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`; present\n/// and reachable → no row.\npub fn audit(surface: &BTreeSet<String>, inv: &Inventory) -> Vec<AuditRow> {\n    let documented: BTreeSet<&String> = inv.surfaces.values().flatten().collect();\n    surface\n        .iter()\n        .filter_map(|token| {\n            if !documented.contains(token) {\n                Some(AuditRow {\n                    token: token.clone(),\n                    code: ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED.to_owned(),\n                })\n            } else if !inv.breadcrumbs.contains(token) {\n                Some(AuditRow {\n                    token: token.clone(),\n                    code: ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE.to_owned(),\n                })\n            } else {\n                None\n            }\n        })\n        .collect()\n}\n\n/// Run the surface step for one configured tool: either record the\n/// `skip` provenance (`surface = \"none\"`), or probe the binary and\n/// harvest its token set. A missing binary is `binary_absent` provenance\n/// — loud, not an error and not a silent skip.\npub fn audit_tool_surface(config: &ToolConfig) -> Result<Provenance, String> {\n    if config.surface_none {\n        return Ok(Provenance {\n            tool: config.tool.clone(),\n            status: \"skip\".to_owned(),\n            detail: \"surface = none: not a --help-probeable CLI surface\".to_owned(),\n            tokens: BTreeSet::new(),\n        });\n    }\n    let binary = config.binary.as_deref().unwrap_or(&config.tool).to_owned();\n    match extract_surface(&binary) {\n        Ok(tokens) => Ok(Provenance {\n            tool: config.tool.clone(),\n            status: \"extracted\".to_owned(),\n            detail: format!(\"{binary} --help\"),\n            tokens,\n        }),\n        Err(_) => Ok(Provenance {\n            tool: config.tool.clone(),\n            status: \"binary_absent\".to_owned(),\n            detail: format!(\"binary '{binary}' not runnable — audit cannot probe its surface\"),\n            tokens: BTreeSet::new(),\n        }),\n    }\n}\n\n/// Canonical form of a feature token: lowercase, alphanumeric\n/// characters only. `--dry-run`, `dry_run`, `Dry Run`, and `dryrun` all\n/// canonicalize to `dryrun` — one feature, one token (design D1).\nfn canonical_raw(s: &str) -> String {\n    s.to_lowercase()\n        .chars()\n        .filter(|c| c.is_ascii_alphanumeric())\n        .collect()\n}\n\n/// Public token normalization: kebab/snake/spacing variants of a\n/// feature name are equivalent. Exposed for contract tests so the\n/// normalization rule itself is pinned, not just its application.\npub fn canonical(s: &str) -> String {\n    canonical_raw(s)\n}\n\n/// Extract the feature-token set from a tool binary's `--help` output:\n/// long flags, subcommand names, and documented exit codes (where the\n/// help lists them), all in canonical form. The binary is invoked with\n/// `--help` and both stdout and stderr are parsed (some CLIs print\n/// usage to stderr even on success).\npub fn extract_surface(binary: &str) -> Result<BTreeSet<String>, String> {\n    let out = Command::new(binary)\n        .arg(\"--help\")\n        .output()\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot run {binary} --help: {e}\"))?;\n    let stdout = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout);\n    let stderr = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr);\n    let mut tokens = harvest_tokens(&stdout);\n    tokens.extend(harvest_tokens(&stderr));\n    Ok(tokens)\n}\n\n/// Harvest feature tokens from help text: long flags, subcommand\n/// entries under a Commands/Subcommands header, and documented exit\n/// codes. General rules only — no tool-specific special cases.\nfn harvest_tokens(help: &str) -> BTreeSet<String> {\n    let mut tokens = BTreeSet::new();\n    let mut in_commands = false;\n    let mut in_exit = false;\n    for line in help.lines() {\n        let trimmed = line.trim();\n        // Long flags: `--flag-name` (strip the dashes, canonicalize).\n        for word in trimmed.split_whitespace() {\n            if let Some(flag) = word.strip_prefix(\"--\") {\n                let flag = flag.split('=').next().unwrap_or(flag);\n                if !flag.is_empty() && flag.chars().any(|c| c.is_ascii_alphanumeric()) {\n                    tokens.insert(canonical_raw(flag));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        // Subcommand section: lines after a `Commands:`/`Subcommands:`\n        // header, until a blank line or non-indented line ends it. The\n        // first word of each indented entry is the subcommand name.\n        if trimmed == \"Commands:\" || trimmed == \"Subcommands:\" {\n            in_commands = true;\n            continue;\n        }\n        if in_commands {\n            if trimmed.is_empty() || !line.starts_with(char::is_whitespace) {\n                in_commands = false;\n            } else if let Some(name) = trimmed\n                .split_whitespace()\n                .next()