commands, long flags, and documented exit codes where `--help`\n   lists them. Token normalization: kebab/snake/spacing variants treated as\n   equivalent (substring-normalized matching per D1).\n2. **Inventory scanner** — scans a repo's docs surfaces (`README.md`,\n   `docs/**`, `llms.txt`, `AGENTS.md` managed blocks) into per-surface\n   feature-token sets.\n3. **Breadcrumb reachability** — a token found in docs but NOT reachable\n   from `llms.txt` or managed-block breadcrumbs → `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`; a\n   token absent from all surfaces → `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`.\n4. **Config** — a checked-in `doc_audit.toml` (tool → repo path, binary\n   name, optional `surface = \"none\"`); `surface: none` tools (e.g. `bd`,\n   `openspec` — not Rust CLIs) skip the binary step and are recorded in\n   provenance, never silently skipped. Absent binaries record provenance\n   `binary_absent` (never silent skip).\n5. **Report wiring** — audit rows flow into the existing report as new\n   check-codes `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED` / `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`;\n   `report_version` stays 1 (additive); `tests/report_aggregation.rs`\n   expectations pass unchanged.\n6. CLI: `evallerina doc-audit` subcommand; wired into `just tier0`.\n\n## Exact files\n- NEW `src/doc_audit.rs` — extractors + scanner + audit rows (MUST carry\n  Purpose header)\n- NEW `doc_audit.toml` — per-tool audit config (all routing.toml tools)\n- `src/lib.rs` — module registration\n- `src/main.rs` — `doc-audit` subcommand + tier-0 wiring\n- `src/report.rs` — accept the two new check-codes (additive only)\n- NEW `tests/doc_audit.rs` — surface + inventory contract tests (failing\n  first); fixture binaries are throwaway shell scripts in a temp dir, NOT\n  real ecosystem binaries\n\n## Red/green sequence\n1. RED: surface test — fixture script prints a `--help` with 2 subcommands +\n   long flags → harvested token set matches, with a kebab/snake pair\n   normalizing to one token. GREEN.\n2. RED: `surface: none` test — tool declared `surface: none` produces no\n   binary probe and records `skip` in provenance. GREEN.\n3. RED: inventory test — fixture repo (temp dir: README + docs/x.md +\n   llms.txt + AGENTS.md managed block) → per-surface token sets. GREEN.\n4. RED: reachability test — token in `docs/x.md` not referenced by\n   `llms.txt`/managed block → `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`; token absent\n   everywhere → `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`; token reachable → no row. GREEN.\n5. RED: `binary_absent` test — configured binary missing → provenance\n   `binary_absent`, loud, not silent. GREEN.\n6. Wire report rows (additive) + CLI + `doc_audit.toml` for the real\n   ecosystem; `just tier0` green. Dogfood check (meter): audit run against\n   evallerina's own surfaces produces a non-empty inventory with zero\n   silent skips.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No routing/filing changes (e4x owns routing audit faults)\n- No new scenario families or tier-2 recordings (vrr/t7n)\n- No report_version bump, no aggregate doc-quality score (anti-goal)\n- No edits to any sibling repo's docs\n\n## Anti-goals\n- Never silently skip a source: every skip is provenance (`skip`,\n  `binary_absent`) — pinned by test\n- No aggregate score field (pinned by test, same discipline as 48g)\n- Token normalization must NOT be tuned to pass evallerina's own docs only\n  (general normalization rules only)\n\n## Commands\n- `cargo test` per red/green step; `just tier0` at end; dogfood:\n  `cargo run -- doc-audit` against evallerina itself → non-empty inventory,\n  zero silent skips\n\n## Follow-up threshold\nIf real-ecosystem audit rows exceed ~40 or the `--help` parsing of any real\ntool resists the extractor (>1h), STOP: record findings as research, ship\nthe mechanism against fixtures, and leave real-tool onboarding notes for\n73q (validation phase). Do not tune normalization to make real rows vanish.\n\n## Verifier evidence contract\nThe verify session's review artifact MUST cite the artifacts it read and\ninclude fresh `cargo test doc_audit` + `just tier0` output before recording\nCONFIRM — otherwise REVIEW_REQUIRED.\n\n## Spawn model\nImplementor: `openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` (matches PI_PROVIDER default);\ncontext ceiling ≤ 50% of its window, computed at spawn.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792528166210},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"Ok7yU5JfT","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/openspec/changes/add-ecosystem-doc-evals/tasks.md","offset":1,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":78519,"output":55,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":78574,"cost":{"input":0.005888925,"output":0.000011000000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0058999249999999994}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792528166213,"responseId":"gen-1792528166-YldNeLJz1Lx21YkTFAGK","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"Ok7yU5JfT","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Tasks: add-ecosystem-doc-evals\n\n## 1. Routing map parity (no battery change)\n\n- [x] 1.1 Failing test: routing-parity parser — fixture README with a\n  MANAGED-TOOLS block + canonical-names table → expected tool→repo pairs\n- [x] 1.2 Implement `routing_parity()` in `src/routing.rs` (or new module):\n  parse sibling ddl README managed block, diff against routing.toml entries,\n  unresolved paths fail, absent sibling → warning\n- [x] 1.3 Wire into tier-0 (`just tier0` / main.rs subcommand) and add\n  `ERR_ROUTING_PARITY` reporting; GHA workflows check out the ddl sibling so\n  the gate enforces in CI (warning-only in local standalone clones)\n- [x] 1.4 Expand routing.toml: testaruda, turu(whisper), ah(espectacular\n  exists), pretender, vampiro, incitaciones, openspec (`upstream = true`),\n  specodelic, funkalization, wild, dulce-de-leche, bd (`upstream = true`);\n  verify parity check green\n\n## 2. Tier-0 doc-coverage audit\n\n- [x] 2.1 Failing test: surface extraction — fixture binary `--help` with\n  subcommands/flags → token set (kebab/snake/spacing normalization)\n- [x] 2.2 Implement surface extractor (`src/doc_audit.rs`: Purpose header per\n  e10 Must gate); `surface: none` fixtures skip cleanly\n- [x] 2.3 Failing test: inventory extraction — fixture repo with README +\n  docs/ + llms.txt + AGENTS.md managed block → feature-token set per surface\n- [x] 2.4 Implement inventory scanner; breadcrumb-reachability check\n  (llms.txt / managed blocks) distinguishing ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED vs\n  ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE\n- [x] 2.5 Wire audit rows into report as new check-codes (report_version\n  stays 1, additive); `just tier0` green\n\n## 3. Routing integration for audit faults\n\n- [ ] 3.1 Failing test: audit row with ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED crosses\n  threshold → dry-run proposal with token `evallerina:<scenario>:<fault-class>`\n- [ ] 3.2 Dry-run smoke against latest tier-2 rows; review proposals before\n  any filing (mirrors 4.3 of add-fault-ticket-routing)\n\n## 4. Doc-findability scenarios (first tools)\n\n- [ ] 4.1 Fixture: turu (whisper) repo slice with llms.txt breadcrumb to a\n  seeded feature doc\n- [ ] 4.2 Record live tier-2 transcript; land scenario JSON + tier-1 replay in\n  same commit (design D5)\n- [ ] 4.3 Repeat for testaruda and ah; step budget + discovery-channel row\n  provenance asserted in replay tests\n\n## 5. Edge-exploration scenarios (first tools)\n\n- [ ] 5.1 Failing test: classifier — non-zero exit without hints on\n  undocumented input → ERR_EDGE_UNHANDLED; hint ignored →\n  ERR_ENVELOPE_HINT_BLINDNESS (existing class)\n- [ ] 5.2 Fixtures + recordings for wai and dont edge inputs (existing battery\n  tools first — cheapest provenance)\n- [ ] 5.3 Extend to turu/testaruda/ah recordings as they land\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n- [ ] 6.1 `just tier0` green; routing-parity + doc-coverage gates pass on this\n  repo itself\n- [ ] 6.2 Dogfood first: run the doc-