"bash","arguments":{"command":"git log --oneline --grep=evallerina-fok --","timeout":null}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":103051,"output":28,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":103079,"cost":{"input":0.007728825,"output":0.000005600000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007734425}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792528326096,"responseId":"gen-1792528326-NZpxI2jK2HpYAXLYDIYL","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"ZG6rPDgkK","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"150f3e2 chore(wai): implement log for evallerina-fok\n5b2bc21 chore(wai): implement log for evallerina-fok\nb049834 chore(wai): evallerina-fok implement-session tracking state\ncc876fd chore(openspec): check off tasks 2.1-2.5 — tier-0 doc-coverage audit landed (evallerina-fok)\ncc880f3 feat(doc-audit): CLI, checked-in config, report wiring, tier-0 line; threshold research for 73q (evallerina-fok step 2.5)\n18d9245 test(doc-audit): binary_absent provenance + hermetic dogfood inventory (evallerina-fok step 2.5 prep)\nc768327 feat(doc-audit): breadcrumb reachability rows ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED / ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE (evallerina-fok step 2.4)\n4f602fe feat(doc-audit): inventory scanner with per-surface token sets + breadcrumbs (evallerina-fok step 2.3)\n5c7f46c feat(doc-audit): surface-none provenance, never a silent skip (evallerina-fok step 2.2)\n838b02a refactor(doc-audit): collapse ifs for clippy -D warnings (evallerina-fok)\nb843636 feat(doc-audit): surface extractor harvests subcommands, flags, exit codes (evallerina-fok step 2.1/2.2)\ncfd8193 chore(wai): brief for evallerina-fok doc-coverage audit\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792528330847},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"A6adxpVO7","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/.wai/projects/evallerina/briefs/evallerina-fok.md","offset":1,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":103478,"output":58,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":103536,"cost":{"input":0.00776085,"output":0.0000116,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007772449999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792528330860,"responseId":"gen-1792528331-fuJOa1FItbE0o4L0SPPh","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"A6adxpVO7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Brief: evallerina-fok — tier-0 doc-coverage audit\n\nTicket: evallerina-fok (P2, complexity:l, lane:afk). Implement the tier-0\ndoc-coverage audit (surface extractor + inventory scanner + audit rows), per\nopenspec change `add-ecosystem-doc-evals` (tasks 2.1–2.5, design D1/D4).\n\n## Why\nBounded pure-Rust module with a crisp TDD shape (harvest tokens → scan docs →\nemit rows) but large breadth: two extractors, a config format, and report\nwiring. Delegation keeps the lead session lean for orchestrating the rest of\nthe epic (phases 3–6 depend on this landing). Independent value: after this\nlands, `just tier0` flags undocumented or unfindable features across the\necosystem the moment docs drift.\n\n## Desired outcome\nNew `src/doc_audit.rs` (Purpose/Responsibilities/Rationale header — e10 Must\ngate) providing:\n1. **Surface extractor** — runs a tool's binary with `--help` (subprocess,\n   in a provisioned fixture sandbox for tests) and harvests a feature-token\n   set: subcommands, long flags, and documented exit codes where `--help`\n   lists them. Token normalization: kebab/snake/spacing variants treated as\n   equivalent (substring-normalized matching per D1).\n2. **Inventory scanner** — scans a repo's docs surfaces (`README.md`,\n   `docs/**`, `llms.txt`, `AGENTS.md` managed blocks) into per-surface\n   feature-token sets.\n3. **Breadcrumb reachability** — a token found in docs but NOT reachable\n   from `llms.txt` or managed-block breadcrumbs → `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`; a\n   token absent from all surfaces → `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`.\n4. **Config** — a checked-in `doc_audit.toml` (tool → repo path, binary\n   name, optional `surface = \"none\"`); `surface: none` tools (e.g. `bd`,\n   `openspec` — not Rust CLIs) skip the binary step and are recorded in\n   provenance, never silently skipped. Absent binaries record provenance\n   `binary_absent` (never silent skip).\n5. **Report wiring** — audit rows flow into the existing report as new\n   check-codes `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED` / `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`;\n   `report_version` stays 1 (additive); `tests/report_aggregation.rs`\n   expectations pass unchanged.\n6. CLI: `evallerina doc-audit` subcommand; wired into `just tier0`.\n\n## Exact files\n- NEW `src/doc_audit.rs` — extractors + scanner + audit rows (MUST carry\n  Purpose header)\n- NEW `doc_audit.toml` — per-tool audit config (all routing.toml tools)\n- `src/lib.rs` — module registration\n- `src/main.rs` — `doc-audit` subcommand + tier-0 wiring\n- `src/report.rs` — accept the two new check-codes (additive only)\n- NEW `tests/doc_audit.rs` — surface + inventory contract tests (failing\n  first); fixture binaries are throwaway shell scripts in a temp dir, NOT\n  real ecosystem binaries\n\n## Red/green sequence\n1. RED: surface test — fixture script prints a `--help` with 2 subcommands +\n   long flags → harvested token set matches, with a kebab/snake pair\n   normalizing to one token. GREEN.\n2. RED: `surface: none` test — tool declared `surface: none` produces no\n   binary probe and records `skip` in provenance. GREEN.\n3. RED: inventory test — fixture repo (temp dir: README + docs/x.md +\n   llms.txt + AGENTS.md managed block) → per-surface token sets. GREEN.\n4. RED: reachability test — token in `docs/x.md` not referenced by\n   `llms.txt`/managed block → `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`; token absent\n   everywhere → `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`; token reachable → no row. GREEN.\n5. RED: `binary_absent` test — configured binary missing → provenance\n   `binary_absent`, loud, not silent. GREEN.\n6. Wire report rows (additive) + CLI + `doc_audit.toml` for the real\n   ecosystem; `just tier0` green. Dogfood check (meter): audit run against\n   evallerina's own surfaces produces a non-empty inventory with zero\n   silent skips.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No routing/filing changes (e4x owns routing audit faults)\n- No new scenario families or tier-2 recordings (vrr/t7n)\n- No report_version bump, no aggregate doc-quality score (anti-goal)\n- No edits to any sibling repo's docs\n\n## Anti-goals\n- Never silently skip a source: every skip is provenance (`skip`,\n  `binary_absent`) — pinned by test\n- No aggregate score field (pinned by test, same discipline as 48g)\n- Token normalization must NOT be tuned to pass evallerina's own docs only\n  (general normalization rules only)\n\n## Commands\n- `cargo test` per red/green step; `just tier0` at end; dogfood:\n  `cargo run -- doc-audit` against evallerina itself → non-empty inventory,\n  zero silent skips\n\n## Follow-up threshold\nIf real-ecosystem audit rows exceed ~40 or the `--help` parsing of any real\ntool resists the extractor (>1h), STOP: record findings as research, ship\nthe mechanism against fixtures, and leave real-tool onboarding notes for\n73q (validation phase). Do not tune normalization to make real rows vanish.\n\n## Verifier evidence contract\nThe verify session's review artifact MUST cite the artifacts it read and\ninclude fresh `cargo test doc_audit` + `just tier0` output before recording\nCONFIRM — otherwise REVIEW_REQUIRED.\n\n## Spawn model\nImplementor: `openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` (matches PI_PROVIDER default);\ncontext ceiling ≤ 50% of its window, computed at spawn.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792528337608},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"pkzDlDTYI","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/openspec/changes/add-ecosystem-doc-evals/tasks.md","offset":1,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":104955,"output":55,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":105010,"cost":{"input":0.007871625,"output":0.000011000000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007882625}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792528337613,"responseId":"gen-1792528337-re9Hn5RoTx6CT8OMKBvj","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"pkzDlDTYI","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Tasks: add-ecosystem-doc-evals\n\n## 1. Routing map parity (no battery change)\n\n- [x] 1.1 Failing test: routing-parity parser — fixture README with a\n  MANAGED-TOOLS block + canonical-names table → expected tool→repo pairs\n- [x] 1.2 Implement `routing_parity()` in `src/routing.rs` (or new module):\n  parse sibling ddl README managed block, diff against routing.toml entries,\n  unresolved paths fail, absent sibling → warning\n- [x] 1.3 Wire into tier-0 (`just tier0` / main.rs subcommand) and add\n  `ERR_ROUTING_PARITY` reporting; GHA workflows check out the ddl sibling so\n  the gate enforces in CI (warning-only in local standalone clones)\n- [x] 1.4 Expand routing.toml: testaruda, turu(whisper), ah(espectacular\n  exists), pretender, vampiro, incitaciones, openspec (`upstream = true`),\n  specodelic, funkalization, wild, dulce-de-leche, bd (`upstream = true`);\n  verify parity check green\n\n## 2. Tier-0 doc-coverage audit\n\n- [x] 2.1 Failing test: surface extraction — fixture binary `--help` with\n  subcommands/flags → token set (kebab/snake/spacing normalization)\n- [x] 2.2 Implement surface extractor (`src/doc_audit.rs`: Purpose header per\n  e10 Must gate); `surface: none` fixtures skip cleanly\n- [x] 2.3 Failing test: inventory extraction — fixture repo with README +\n  docs/ + llms.txt + AGENTS.md managed block → feature-token set per surface\n- [x] 2.4 Implement inventory scanner; breadcrumb-reachability check\n  (llms.txt / managed blocks) distinguishing ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED vs\n  ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE\n- [x] 2.5 Wire audit rows into report as new check-codes (report_version\n  stays 1, additive); `just tier0` green\n\n## 3. Routing integration for audit faults\n\n- [ ] 3.1 Failing test: audit row with ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED crosses\n  threshold → dry-run proposal with token `evallerina:<scenario>:<fault-class>`\n- [ ] 3.2 Dry-run smoke against latest tier-2 rows; review proposals before\n  any filing (mirrors 4.3 of add-fault-ticket-routing)\n\n## 4. Doc-findability scenarios (first tools)\n\n- [ ] 4.1 Fixture: turu (whisper) repo slice with llms.txt breadcrumb to a\n  seeded feature doc\n- [ ] 4.2 Record live tier-2 transcript; land scenario JSON + tier-1 replay in\n  same commit (design D5)\n- [ ] 4.3 Repeat for testaruda and ah; step budget + discovery-channel row\n  provenance asserted in replay tests\n\n## 5. Edge-exploration scenarios (first tools)\n\n- [ ] 5.1 Failing test: classifier — non-zero exit without hints on\n  undocumented input → ERR_EDGE_UNHANDLED; hint ignored →\n  ERR_ENVELOPE_HINT_BLINDNESS (existing class)\n- [ ] 5.2 Fixtures + recordings for wai and dont edge inputs (existing battery\n  tools first — cheapest provenance)\n- [ ] 5.3 Extend to turu/testaruda/ah recordings as they land\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n- [ ] 6.1 `just tier0` green; routing-parity + doc-coverage gates pass on this\n  repo itself\n- [ ] 6.2 Dogfood first: run the doc-coverage audit against evallerina's own\n  surfaces (README, docs/, AGENTS.md) before any tool-fixture rollout —\n  fastest way to shake out the extractor\n- [ ] 6.3 `just tier1` replay unchanged for existing scenarios\n- [ ] 6.4 One full nightly rotation green with new families; dry-run\n  proposals reviewed; `--file` remains opt-in\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792528350496},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"2GSNSaLB3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/.wai/projects/evallerina/research/2026-10-20-evallerina-fok-real-ecosystem-audit-breadth.md","offset":1,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":105972,"output":78,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":106050,"cost":{"input":0.007947899999999999,"output":0.0000156,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007963499999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792528350507,"responseId":"gen-1792528350-yL4cQfbmx0yqoi1SrHz5","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"2GSNSaLB3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research: evallerina-fok — real-ecosystem doc-audit rows exceed follow-up threshold\n\nDate: 2026-10-20 · Ticket: evallerina-fok · Trigger: brief follow-up threshold\n(\"real-ecosystem audit rows exceed ~40 → STOP, record findings, ship mechanism\nagainst fixtures, leave onboarding notes for 73q\").\n\n## Finding\n\n`cargo run -- doc-audit` against the checked-in `doc_audit.toml` yields **91\naudit rows** across 9 tools (threshold ~40). Breakdown:\n\n- `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`: 77 rows — token documented on some surface but not\n  reachable from llms.txt / AGENTS.md managed-block breadcrumbs. Dominant\n  pattern: most repos document commands/flags in README/docs but have no\n  breadcrumb channel (no llms.txt, or llms.txt that doesn't enumerate the\n  feature). This is the *intended* signal of the gate, not extractor noise.\n- `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`: 14 rows — e.g. `dont color/forget/nopersist/quiet/\n  stats`, `turu quiet/verbose/help`, `specodelic verbose/exit1`, `ah help`,\n  `vampiro completions`, `incitaciones dir`, `pretender help`.\n\nProvenance (16/16 tools accounted, **zero silent skips**): 10 `extracted`,\n4 `binary_absent` (genesis, espectacular, funkalization, dulce-de-leche —\nbinaries not on PATH in this checkout), 2 `skip` (bd, openspec —\n`surface = none` by config).\n\nNo tool's `--help` resisted parsing — the general extractor rules (long flags,\nCommands: sections, exit-code sections) harvested all 10 present binaries\nwithout tool-specific cases. The threshold tripped on breadth (row count), not\nparse resistance.\n\n## Decision (per brief)\n\n- Do NOT tune normalization to make real rows vanish (anti-goal).\n- The mechanism ships against fixtures; all contract tests are hermetic\n  (throwaway shell scripts + temp repos). `cargo test` green.\n- Real-tool onboarding for 73q (validation phase): see notes below.\n- The CLI exits 0 on findings — rows are the record (mirrors `report`\n  precedent: findings do not affect the exit code; loud errors exit nonzero).\n  Rows print on every `just tier0` run, so drift is surfaced immediately.\n\n## Onboarding notes for 73q\n\n1. **binary_absent tools**: build/install `genesis`, `espectacular`,\n   `funkalization`, `dulce-de-leche` binaries on PATH (or\n   extend `doc_audit.toml` with explicit `binary` paths into their\n   `target/`) so their surfaces join the audit.\n2. **NOT_FINDABLE triage**: 77 rows mostly mean \"add an llms.txt breadcrumb or\n   managed-block mention per feature\". Recommend each repo owner add an\n   llms.txt enumerating commands/flags; then rows collapse to genuinely\n   undocumented tokens.\n3. **Noise class**: clap auto-generates a `help` subcommand/flag; it shows up\n   as UNDOCUMENTED when docs don't mention \"help\". If 73q wants to suppress\n   it, that should be a *general* normalization decision recorded here — not\n   per-tool tuning.\n4. **Gate posture**: doc-audit rows do not fail `just tier0` (measurement,\n   not gate). If the epic wants a gate later, add a threshold/scoped-gate\n   decision to a follow-up ticket — do not silently tune the extractor.\n\n## Artifacts read/produced\n\n- Produced: `src/doc_audit.rs`, `doc_audit.toml`, `tests/doc_audit.rs`,\n  report wiring in `src/report.rs`, CLI in `src/main.rs`, justfile tier-0 line.\n- Fresh evidence: `cargo test doc_audit` (8 passed) and `just tier0` tails in\n  the evallerina-fok ship record.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792528359431},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"L92PW0DH1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/src/report.rs","offset":1,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":106989,"output":44,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":107033,"cost":{"input":0.008024175,"output":0.0000088,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.008032975}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792528359433,"responseId":"gen-1792528360-WzzLo6DfaBLfcqxk2Vay","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"L92PW0DH1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"//! Purpose: Tier-1/2 report aggregation into the per-channel fault\n//! dashboard (evallerina-48g).\n//! Responsibilities: aggregate report_version 1 rows (tier-2 rotation\n//! events and tier-1 rows without model attribution) into a\n//! per-output-channel × check-code × model-id fault matrix, apply the\n//! evals-guidelines fault routing (tool faults → tool tickets; agent\n//! faults → AIX-channel work only at the cross-model threshold),\n//! surface absent, rate_limited, and http_error cells as coverage\n//! records — never failures, never dropped — and refuse loudly on unmappable scenarios\n//! instead of silently bucketing them.\n//! Rationale: evals-guidelines \"Fault routing\" and \"suite-wide\n//! aggregation\" requirements. The dashboard deliberately carries no\n//! single aggregate score: per-capability breakdown is a hard\n//! requirement, and a collapse into one number hides exactly the\n//! channel × code × model signal the routing rule needs.\n\nuse serde_json::json;\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};\n\n/// Validate the `report` subcommand's routing flags: `--file` (cross-repo\n/// write authorization, Phase 2) requires `--route` — filing proposed\n/// tickets only makes sense after the routing step ran. Any combination\n/// without `--file` is fine.\npub fn validate_route_flags(route: bool, file: bool) -> Result<(), String> {\n    if file && !route {\n        return Err(\n            \"--file requires --route: filing proposed tickets only makes sense after the routing step ran\".into(),\n        );\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// The scenario definition's recorded tool — the repo key for routing\n/// (routing.rs keys proposals on this, never the report row's `tool`\n/// field, which is hardcoded for live trials). Scenario names\n/// prefix-encode the eval target by convention (`wai-*`, `dont-*`);\n/// an unknown prefix is None → a loud error downstream (never a\n/// silent bucket, mirroring aggregate_rows).\npub fn scenario_tool_of(name: &str) -> Option<String> {\n    if name.starts_with(\"wai-\") {\n        Some(\"wai\".to_owned())\n    } else if name.starts_with(\"dont-\") {\n        Some(\"dont\".to_owned())\n    } else {\n        None\n    }\n}\n\n/// Run the routing step against an aggregated dashboard: propose\n/// dry-run tickets from the same rows the dashboard aggregated from,\n/// optionally file them (Phase 2, `--file`), and attach the additive\n/// `routed` summary — decision counts only, no aggregate score — to\n/// the dashboard JSON.\n///\n/// Returns the proposals so the caller can serialize\n/// proposed-tickets.jsonl. Routing never affects the exit code unless\n/// it errors loudly (empty registry, unknown scenario, version\n/// mismatch): skipped proposals (unmapped tool, bd failure) are the\n/// record, not failures.\npub fn attach_routing(\n    dashboard: &mut serde_json::Value,\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    repo_map: &BTreeMap<String, String>,\n    file_authorized: bool,\n    run_bd: &mut crate::routing::BdRunner,\n) -> Result<Vec<crate::routing::ProposalRow>, String> {\n    let mut proposals =\n        crate::routing::propose(rows, configured_models, &scenario_tool_of, repo_map)?;\n    crate::routing::file_proposals(&mut proposals, file_authorized, run_bd)?;\n\n    let (mut filed, mut existing, mut dry_run, mut skipped) = (0usize, 0, 0, 0);\n    for p in &proposals {\n        match p.decision.as_str() {\n            \"filed\" => filed += 1,\n            \"existing\" => existing += 1,\n            \"dry_run\" => dry_run += 1,\n            _ => skipped += 1,\n        }\n    }\n    dashboard[\"routed\"] = json!({\n        \"filed\": filed,\n        \"existing\": existing,\n        \"dry_run\": dry_run,\n        \"skipped\": skipped,\n    });\n    Ok(proposals)\n}\n\n/// The full CLI routing step for `report --route`: load routing.toml\n/// (from the current directory — the repo root on rotation day),\n/// attach the routed summary to the dashboard, and write\n/// proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the report file. `file_authorized`\n/// comes from the explicit `--file` flag; the runner is injectable so\n/// tests can spy on bd calls.\npub fn run_routing_step(\n    dashboard: &mut serde_json::Value,\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    report_path: &std::path::Path,\n    file_authorized: bool,\n    run_bd: &mut crate::routing::BdRunner,\n) -> Result<Vec<crate::routing::ProposalRow>, String> {\n    let content = std::fs::read_to_string(\"routing.toml\")\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot read routing.toml: {e}\"))?;\n    let repo_map = crate::routing::parse_routing_toml(&content)?;\n    let proposals = attach_routing(\n        dashboard,\n        rows,\n        configured_models,\n        &repo_map,\n        file_authorized,\n        run_bd,\n    )?;\n    let jsonl = crate::routing::to_jsonl(&proposals);\n    let out_path = report_path\n        .parent()\n        .unwrap_or(std::path::Path::new(\".\"))\n        .join(\"proposed-tickets.jsonl\");\n    std::fs::write(&out_path, jsonl)\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot write {}: {e}\", out_path.display()))?;\n    Ok(proposals)\n}\n\n/// Version of the dashboard shape. Additive evolution only within a\n/// version; breaking changes bump this.\npub const DASHBOARD_VERSION: u32 = 1;\n\n/// The evals-guidelines cross-model routing threshold for agent faults\n/// within one output channel.\nconst ROUTING_THRESHOLD: usize = 3;\n\n/// The output channel a live scenario's checks probe (the fault-routing\n/// key per evals-guidelines: suggestions, envelope, managed-block, or\n/// artifact surface). Registered for every live scenario; the channel\n/// must exist before rotation day, not after the first dashboard run.\npub fn scenario_channel(name: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {\n    match name {\n        \"wai-hint-adherence-smoke\"\n        | \"wai-hint-adherence-corrupt-config\"\n        | \"dont-hint-adherence-lifecycle\" => Some(\"envelope\"),\n        \"wai-hint-adherence-typo\" => Some(\"suggestions\"),\n        \"wai-doc-drift-stale-agents-md\" | \"dont-doc-drift-stale-lifecycle\" => Some(\"artifact\"),\n        // Archetype family (evallerina-bhh): vampiro-polyglot-seam asserts\n        // on vampiro's gate/guidance JSON envelopes; wai-drifted-ecosystem\n        // probes the stale-AGENTS.md artifact via doc_drift_blindness,\n        // mapping to `artifact` like its doc-drift siblings.\n        \"vampiro-polyglot-seam\" => Some(\"envelope\"),\n        \"wai-drifted-ecosystem\" => Some(\"artifact\"),\n        // Tier-0 doc-coverage audit rows (evallerina-fok, additive:\n        // report_version stays 1) probe the `docs` channel — feature\n        // documentation is the output channel the audit checks.\n        \"doc-audit\" => Some(\"docs\"),\n        _ => None,\n    }\n}\n\n/// One accumulator key in the routing maps: agent faults key on\n/// (channel, code), tool faults on (tool, check, channel) because they\n/// carry no code by contract.\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord)]\nenum FaultKey {\n    /// Agent fault: the `ERR_*` taxonomy code within one output channel.\n    Agent { channel: String, code: String },\n    /// Tool fault: no code; routed to the tool's repository.\n    Tool {\n        tool: String,\n        check: String,\n        channel: String,\n    },\n}\n\n/// Accumulated occurrences for one fault key: total count plus the set\n/// of distinct model ids observed (empty for non-tier-2 rows).\n#[derive(Debug, Default)]\nstruct FaultTally {\n    occurrences: usize,\n    models: BTreeSet<String>,\n    scenarios: BTreeSet<String>,\n}\n\n/// Aggregate report_version 1 rows into the dashboard JSON.\n///\n/// `rows` are parsed report rows as [`serde_json::Value`]: tier-2\n/// rotation events (`kind: trial | absent`) or tier-1 rows without a\n/// `model` field (grouped as non-tier-2 per the report contract).\n/// `configured_models` is the model registry the rotation was\n/// configured with — it defines the routing threshold (3, or the full\n/// registry size when fewer than three are configured). `channel_of`\n/// resolves a scenario to the output channel its checks probe; an\n/// unknown scenario is a loud error, never a silent bucket.\n///\n/// The returned value is the serialized dashboard shape: no single\n/// aggregate score, per-capability breakdown only.\npub fn aggregate_rows(\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    channel_of: &dyn Fn(&str) -> Option<&'static str>,\n) -> Result<serde_json::Value, String> {\n    if configured_models.is_empty() {\n\n[275 more lines in file. Use offset=201 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792528365177},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"zgQe11xHC","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/src/main.rs","offset":201,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":109165,"output":45,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":109210,"cost":{"input":0.008187375,"output":0.000009,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.008196375}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792528365186,"responseId":"gen-1792528365-QQ5esgY48bDrmk4NnbEp","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"zgQe11xHC","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"            &scenario,\n            reps,\n            model,\n            dry_run,\n            real_artifacts,\n            budget_mins,\n            &out,\n        ) {\n            Ok(code) => code,\n            Err(msg) => {\n                eprintln!(\"{msg}\");\n                ExitCode::FAILURE\n            }\n        },\n    }\n}\n\n/// Tier-2 live rotation: the scenario battery (or one named scenario)\n/// × selected models × reps, in registry order, under a per-run\n/// wall-clock budget. One JSON event per cell on stdout — a\n/// report_version 1 trial row or an absent record. Exit nonzero iff a\n/// trial failed or malformed; rate-limited and budget-skipped cells are\n/// recorded in their rows, they are not failures (the row is the\n/// record).\nfn run_live(\n    scenario: Option<String>,\n    reps: u32,\n    model: Option<String>,\n    budget_mins: u64,\n) -> Result<ExitCode, String> {\n    let scenarios: Vec<_> = match scenario {\n        Some(name) => vec![live_scenario_by_name(&name)?],\n        None => live_scenarios(),\n    };\n    let models: Vec<String> = match model {\n        Some(id) => vec![id],\n        None => ordered_ids().into_iter().map(String::from).collect(),\n    };\n    let start = Instant::now();\n    let budget = Duration::from_secs(budget_mins * 60);\n    let mut factory = |m: &str| {\n        OpenRouterTransport::from_env(m)\n            .map(|t| Box::new(t) as Box<dyn evallerina::live::Transport>)\n    };\n    let events = run_rotation(\n        &scenarios,\n        &models,\n        reps,\n        &mut factory,\n        &evallerina::live::Bounds::default(),\n        &|| start.elapsed() < budget,\n    )?;\n    let mut trial_failed = false;\n    for event in &events {\n        if let RotationEvent::Trial { report } = event {\n            trial_failed |= matches!(\n                report.status,\n                TrialStatus::Failed | TrialStatus::InvalidOutput\n            );\n        }\n        println!(\"{}\", serde_json::to_string(event).unwrap());\n    }\n    if trial_failed {\n        Ok(ExitCode::FAILURE)\n    } else {\n        Ok(ExitCode::SUCCESS)\n    }\n}\n\n/// Tier-0 routing-map parity gate (evallerina-0sy): read the checked-in\n/// routing.toml and the ddl sibling README relative to the repo root\n/// (discovered worktree-safe), run\n/// [`evallerina::routing_parity::routing_parity`], and print the parity\n/// report as JSON. Exit nonzero\n/// iff any parity row failed (`ERR_ROUTING_PARITY` rows carry tool +\n/// detail); an absent ddl sibling degrades to a warning row with exit\n/// 0 — parse failures stay loud and nonzero.\nfn run_routing_parity() -> Result<ExitCode, String> {\n    let root = evallerina::routing::discover_root()?;\n    let root_path = std::path::PathBuf::from(&root);\n    let toml_path = root_path.join(\"routing.toml\");\n    let toml = std::fs::read_to_string(&toml_path)\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot read {}: {e}\", toml_path.display()))?;\n    let readme_path = root_path.join(evallerina::routing_parity::DDL_README);\n    let readme = std::fs::read_to_string(&readme_path).ok();\n    let report = evallerina::routing_parity::routing_parity(readme.as_deref(), &toml, &root_path)?;\n    println!(\n        \"{}\",\n        serde_json::to_string_pretty(&report.to_json()).expect(\"parity report serializes\")\n    );\n    if report.failed() {\n        Ok(ExitCode::FAILURE)\n    } else {\n        Ok(ExitCode::SUCCESS)\n    }\n}\n\n/// Tier-0 doc-coverage audit CLI handler (evallerina-fok): load the\n/// checked-in doc_audit.toml from the repo root, run the surface step\n/// per tool (binary probe, or `skip`/`binary_absent` provenance —\n/// never a silent skip), scan each tool's local repo surfaces into a\n/// doc inventory, and diff the two into per-token audit rows that also\n/// flow into the report contract as report_version 1 rows. Findings\n/// are the record, not gate failures (the dashboard is the record);\n/// nonzero exit is reserved for loud errors: missing/malformed config,\n/// unreadable surfaces.\nfn run_doc_audit() -> Result<ExitCode, String> {\n    let root = evallerina::routing::discover_root()?;\n    let root_path = std::path::PathBuf::from(&root);\n    let config_path = root_path.join(\"doc_audit.toml\");\n    let config_src = std::fs::read_to_string(&config_path)\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot read {}: {e}\", config_path.display()))?;\n    let configs = evallerina::doc_audit::parse_config(&config_src)?;\n\n    let mut provenance = Vec::new();\n    let mut tools = serde_json::Map::new();\n    let mut report_rows = Vec::new();\n    let mut audit_rows_all = Vec::new();\n    for config in &configs {\n        let prov = evallerina::doc_audit::audit_tool_surface(config)?;\n        let mut tool_json = serde_json::json!({\n            \"surface_status\": prov.status,\n            \"surface_tokens\": prov.tokens.len(),\n            \"audit_rows\": 0,\n        });\n        if !prov.tokens.is_empty() {\n            // Only tools with a harvested surface can produce audit\n            // rows; the repo must be a local checkout to scan.\n            let repo = evallerina::routing::resolve_repo(&config.repo, &root_path);\n            let repo_path = std::path::PathBuf::from(&repo);\n            if repo_path.is_dir() {\n                let inv = evallerina::doc_audit::scan_inventory(&repo_path)?;\n                let rows = evallerina::doc_audit::audit(&prov.tokens, &inv);\n                tool_json[\"surfaces\"] = serde_json::json!(inv.surfaces.len());\n                tool_json[\"audit_rows\"] = serde_json::json!(rows.len());\n                audit_rows_all.extend(rows.iter().map(\n                    |r| serde_json::json!({\"tool\": config.tool, \"token\": r.token, \"code\": r.code}),\n                ));\n                if !rows.is_empty() {\n                    report_rows.push(evallerina::doc_audit::report_row(&config.tool, &rows));\n                }\n            } else {\n                provenance.push(serde_json::json!({\n                    \"tool\": config.tool,\n                    \"status\": \"repo_absent\",\n                    \"detail\": format!(\"repo checkout '{repo}' not found — inventory not scanned\"),\n                }));\n                tool_json[\"surfaces\"] = serde_json::json!(0);\n            }\n        }\n        provenance.push(serde_json::json!({\n            \"tool\": prov.tool,\n            \"status\": prov.status,\n            \"detail\": prov.detail,\n        }));\n        tools.insert(config.tool.clone(), tool_json);\n    }\n\n    println!(\n        \"{}\",\n        serde_json::to_string_pretty(&serde_json::json!({\n            \"inventory\": tools,\n            \"provenance\": provenance,\n            \"audit_rows\": audit_rows_all,\n            \"report_rows\": report_rows,\n        }))\n        .expect(\"doc-audit report serializes\")\n    );\n    Ok(ExitCode::SUCCESS)\n}\n\n/// Aggregate a JSONL file of report rows into the fault dashboard.\n/// The configured model registry comes from the checked-in registry;\n/// the channel map from the live scenario registry. Findings do not\n/// affect the exit code — the dashboard is the record, and nonzero\n/// exits are reserved for aggregation errors.\nfn run_report(path: &str, route: bool, file: bool) -> Result<ExitCode, String> {\n    evallerina::report::validate_route_flags(route, file)?;\n    let content = std::fs::read_to_string(path)\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot read report rows from {path}: {e}\"))?;\n    let rows: Vec<serde_json::Value> = content\n        .lines()\n        .filter(|line| !line.trim().is_empty())\n        .map(|line| serde_json::from_str(line).map_err(|e| format!(\"malformed report row: {e}\")))\n        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, String>>()?;\n    let configured: Vec<String> = ordered_ids().into_iter().map(String::from).collect();\n    let mut dashboard = evallerina::report::aggregate_rows(\n        &rows,\n        &configured,\n        &evallerina::report::scenario_channel,\n    )?;\n    if route {\n        let mut runner = evallerina::routing::run_bd;\n        evallerina::report::run_routing_step(\n            &mut dashboard,\n            &rows,\n            &configured,\n            std::path::Path::new(path),\n            file,\n            &mut runner,\n\n[114 more lines in file. Use offset=401 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792528370860},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"Y7RCfNP1Z","name":"read","arguments":{"function":"bash","parameters":{"command":"git log --oneline --grep=evallerina-fok --","timeout":null}}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":111260,"output":37,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":111297,"cost":{"input":0.0083445,"output":0.0000074,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.008351899999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792528370865,"responseId":"gen-1792528371-pdInqrdK6xGL1Fio72fl","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"Y7RCfNP1Z","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Validation failed for tool \"read\":\n  - path: must have required properties path\n\nReceived arguments:\n{\n  \"function\": \"bash\",\n  \"parameters\": {\n    \"command\": \"git log --oneline --grep=evallerina-fok --\",\n    \"timeout\": null\n  }\n}"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1792528376454},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"xmSvz7hDq","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"git log --oneline --gre